BEGIN_HYPERDESC
<h1>Floating</h1>
A delta-glider (gear down, some fuel, and full tanks) and a ShuttlePB are
let go just above the open Atlantic on a calm sea (no wind: no swell).
They must come to float upright at rest, at the draft their weight sets,
neither sinking to the seabed nor bobbing on.
END_HYPERDESC

BEGIN_ENVIRONMENT
  System Sol
  Date MJD 51982.6685767396
  Script Tests/WaterFloatTest
END_ENVIRONMENT

BEGIN_FOCUS
  Ship DG
END_FOCUS

BEGIN_CAMERA
  TARGET DG
  MODE Extern
  POS 4 0 -20
  TRACKMODE TargetRelative
  FOV 50.00
END_CAMERA

BEGIN_SHIPS
DG:DeltaGlider
  STATUS Landed Earth
  POS -70.0000 28.0000
  HEADING 90.00
  GEAR 1 1.0000
  PRPLEVEL 0:0.200 1:1.000
END
DGFULL:DeltaGlider
  STATUS Landed Earth
  POS -70.0030 28.0000
  HEADING 90.00
  GEAR 0 0.0000
  PRPLEVEL 0:1.000 1:1.000
END
PB:ShuttlePB
  STATUS Landed Earth
  POS -70.0015 28.0020
  HEADING 0.00
  PRPLEVEL 0:0.500
END
END_SHIPS
